{# ---------- Philosophy ---------- #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="philosophy-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our philosophy</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="philosophy-title">Leave to Learn. Return to Lead.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Global experience enriches your social work practice and expands your career opportunities. Our international partnerships provide unique learning environments to understand social issues in diverse cultural contexts.</p>
        <p>Social work looks different in a Santiago hospital, an Oaxaca feminist collective, a Wellington counseling center, a Cape Town child welfare agency or a UNHCR desk in Geneva. Learning alongside practitioners in those settings teaches what no classroom can: how culture shapes need, how communities organize their own solutions and how to practice with humility when you are the outsider.</p>
        <p>That is why the School has placed students internationally since 1993, when the first interns joined UNHCR in Geneva. In the decades since, students have been placed on every continent except Antarctica and faculty-led internships for MSSW students have run in 20 countries. Global engagement has been part of the School's signature education landscape for more than 20 years.</p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><strong>Cross-cultural competence.</strong> Develop the cross-cultural competence essential for today's interconnected world, whether your career takes you overseas or to a Texas community that is global in its own right.</li>
          <li><strong>Career outcomes.</strong> Immersive practicum experience with international agencies, from grassroots organizations to a United Nations body, sets graduates apart in clinical, policy and leadership roles.</li>
          <li><strong>Learning from practitioners worldwide.</strong> Every program pairs students with experienced social workers and community leaders who teach from their own context, not ours.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="split__media">
        <blockquote class="pullquote">When a member of our social work community engages globally, we believe they leave to learn and return to lead.</blockquote>
        <figcaption class="pullquote-cite">Noël Busch-Armendariz, Ph.D., Associate Dean for Global Engagement</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

