{# ---------- How OGE supports you ---------- #}
<section class="section section--sand" aria-labelledby="support-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="support-title">How OGE supports you</h2>
        <p class="section__intro">You do not go alone. The Office of Global Engagement works with faculty, the School's practicum office and Texas Global so that every student is prepared, placed and supported from first conversation to return.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-list feature-list--2">
      <li><strong>Advising.</strong> Talk with OGE staff early about which program fits your degree plan, interests and timeline. We help you weigh options before you commit.</li>
      <li><strong>Faculty liaisons.</strong> Each global practicum site has a designated faculty liaison who knows the agencies, the city and the work: Anita Guajardo (Santiago and Oaxaca), Starla Simmons (Wellington), Tammy Linseisen (Cape Town) and Assistant Dean Stacey Jordan (UNHCR). Have questions about a specific agency or program? Reach out to the liaison associated with it.</li>
      <li><strong>Global Practicum Seminar.</strong> International interns take the Global Practicum Seminar, taught by Assistant Dean Tanya Voss, to connect their placement to social work theory and to one another across time zones.</li>
      <li><strong>Coordination with the Office of Practicum Education and Texas Global.</strong> OGE coordinates with the School's Office of Practicum Education and UT's Texas Global to offer advanced Clinical and APP practicums each spring, so your placement meets degree requirements and university travel standards.</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-departure preparation.</strong> Information sessions, application guidance and pre-departure preparation cover logistics, expectations and cultural orientation before you leave.</li>
      <li><strong>A community when you return.</strong> Returning students share their experience through Global Stories and campus showcases, and help the next cohort decide to go.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

